  "details": "The Big Menu will recenter to be in front of you in VR when you are teleported, regardless of how that teleport was made. \n\nFor game worlds that use teleporting to assist with movement or attach you to an object it becomes annoying with the Big Menu stuck to your face since the world is performing teleports every frame.\n\nSuggestion:\n\nThere is a Lerp On Remote flag that can be enabled to allow a player to slide to their next position over the network. It would be handy if this also disabled the recentering of the Big Menu.\n\nI do understand that there is a possibility of a world to abuse this and \"soft lock\" the player by teleporting them in a spinning motion but this could be resolved a bit by having the Big Menu follow the teleport motion. I feel that these issues would be small in comparison to the removal of the annoyance that is to use the Big Menu while in a world that uses teleporting multiple times a second.",
